3. Summary of Findings:

Key Insights from SQL Queries:
The SQL queries provided accurate aggregation of order and sales data, helping identify trends and areas for improvement.
The segmentation of customers and the grouping by order and payment statuses allowed us to pinpoint issues and opportunities in various operational areas.
Observations from Customer Retention Analysis:
The cohort retention heatmap indicates that while a solid base of customers makes repeat purchases, the retention rates drop significantly in subsequent months.
The data suggests that new customers have strong initial engagement, which tapers off, highlighting an opportunity for targeted re-engagement strategies.
Recommendations for Alt Mobility:
Enhance customer engagement with follow-up communications or loyalty programs shortly after the first purchase.
Refine marketing strategies to target high-risk cohorts and try to increase the conversion of repeat purchases.
Improve payment processes identified in the SQL analysis to ensure a seamless customer experience and reduce drop-offs.
